    {
      "question": "The card's due-date half: should an object-bound timeline ever head a past date 'Overdue' (an open, past-due record on a due-date axis, never a closed one), and through which DECLARED signal? Today nothing the timeline reads declares a due-date role or a closed record, so the second pin cannot be built without inventing one.",
      "options": [
        "A. No timeline 'Overdue'. The bucket stays calendar position only (Earlier/Today/...), and timeline.bucket.overdue retires from the defaults row and all ten packs in a small follow-up, which the card then closes on. REAL NEED (measured): zero producers of a due-date timeline. The only in-tree timeline configs are the showcase's created_at timeline and its copy in objectstack lint fixtures; no objectstack example and no console face binds a due date. The overdue judgement already lives where record state lives: the dueLike date cell (red text plus 'Overdue Nd'), the gantt's server-computed borderColorField alert, conditional formatting. LONG-TERM: the bucket is a fact the timeline owns (where the date falls), while overdue is record state owned by fields and the server; no workaround. AI-SAFETY: nothing to declare, so nothing an AI can mis-declare or have hidden by a heuristic. STARTUP SCOPE: zero new surface, and the dead key retires at once with no staged window. Cost: a hypothetical due-date timeline outside this tree loses its 'Overdue' header (no named external user).",
