        "C. Reuse objectui's existing dueLike affordance (the object-field dueLike key plus @object-ui/fields' field-name regex) and a status-value token heuristic for 'closed'. REAL NEED: it would fire only on showcase-shaped names. LONG-TERM: a second dialect; dueLike is not a spec FieldSchema key, so a platform-served object cannot carry it and only the name regex would ever fire. AI-SAFETY: the worst option, because guesses read like declarations and hide naming mistakes, and the card itself rules out guessing field names. STARTUP SCOPE: no new spec surface, but a wider heuristic surface."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, on all four axes: measured zero pull for a due-date timeline; overdue is record state that the field cell and the server already judge; nothing new for an AI to mis-author; and it retires a key with zero call sites at once instead of growing a declared surface. If the maintainer wants the capability later, B is the only correct route, and it starts in the spec."
